<title>GERMANY: Jungheinrich five-month sales grow.</title>
<headline>Jungheinrich five-month sales grow.</headline>
<dateline>HAMBURG, Germany 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>German fork-lift maker Jungheinrich AG said on Monday its sales grew 3.6 percent to 954 million marks in the first five months of 1997, compared with the year-earlier period.</p>
<p>Chairman Hans-Peter Schmohl told the company's annual general meeting that incoming orders rose to 340 million marks from 315 million marks</p>
<p>Developments in the first half have been in line with expectations, and the company aims to post a profit of over 30 million marks this year, he said.</p>
<p>In 1996, Jungheinrich posted a net loss of 19.7 million marks on sales of 2.41 billion marks. The company said the loss was mainly due to one-time costs for personnel reductions.</p>
<p>-- Terence Gallagher, Bonn newsroom, 49-228-2609750</p>
